"""gemm_skinny native-layout configuration tables (generated; do not edit by hand).

Generated from LightGBM surrogates of measured data per arch: the gemm_skinny
configuration searches on NN / TN / TT shapes (MN-contiguous operands read in
place), the RCR configuration searches (gfx950), and the dispatcher's
per-shape timings. For every bin ``(layout, M <= N, MN leading
dimension odd, floor(log2 min(M, N)) in 0..9, floor(log2 max(M, N)) in 7..15,
floor(log2 K) in 6..15)`` a table holds the configuration with the lowest
predicted time at the bin-center shape, over the candidate grid (atoms, wave
split, K chunk, prefetch depth, waves target of the split-K degree).

Entry: ``(wave_m_atoms, wave_n_atoms, warp_m, warp_n, warp_k, kc, prefetch,
waves_target, r, rx)``; ``waves_target`` 0 = no split-K, else the split-K
degree is chosen at dispatch to reach about that many waves; ``r`` = 100 x
the predicted time ratio hipBLASLt-best / this configuration, ``rx`` = 100 x
the predicted ratio hipBLASLt-best / the dispatcher's non-gemm_skinny pick
(the admission compares the two).
"""

